source: tests/cli.rs
expression: "String::from_utf8_lossy(&help.get_output().stdout)"
---
Short-lived AWS credentials through IAM Identity Center.

gac logs you in, keeps native sso-session profiles in ~/.aws/config in step with your account and
role assignments, and shares its token cache with the AWS CLI and SDKs.

Usage: gac [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  setup        Create an [sso-session], or reuse one `aws configure sso` already wrote
  login        Sign in to IAM Identity Center and write the shared token cache
  logout       Revoke the session, delete its cached token and the AWS CLI's SSO role credentials
  select       Pick the account and role of the [default] profile from a list
  status       Show sessions, token and registration expiry, and managed blocks. No secrets
  sync         Write native sso-session profiles for your accounts and roles into a managed block
  list         List the accounts and roles you can use
  exec         Run a command with a role's credentials in its environment
  doctor       Check the AWS files and caches for problems; --fix applies the mechanical fixes
  completions  Print a shell completion script, e.g. `source <(gac completions zsh)`
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Global options:
      --session <NAME>
          The [sso-session] to use, overriding the session of the [default] profile
          
          [env: GAC_REDUX_SESSION]

      --no-input
          Never prompt; fail with a hint instead

  -v, --verbose...
          Log to stderr: -v for debug, -vv for trace. Secrets are never logged
